# Panic-by-default preserved: an UNCAUGHT out-of-bounds array index still halts
# the program — post-D11/T2b it emits the normative `trap[T_Bounds]: index out of
# bounds: index 10, length 3 at <file>:<line>:<col>` and exits 101 (the flagship
# `v[i]` READ carries a real source location) — the Fault.Bounds machinery must
# not perturb the plain index-read path (error-model.md §11).
void main():
    Vector[int] xs = [10, 20, 30]
    int r = xs[10]
    print(f"{r}")
